Notes on the red and green runs (faults in the tests of this lane, not weakened claims):
- item 1: the first run of life_cycle_resid_set_swap_identical failed 1 check: the test expected
  adf_resid_is_canonical(y) == 0 after adf_resid_set_fmpz2(y, -3, 7), which reduces c into [0, m) and
  gives P(7, 4). The test was wrong; it now writes -3 into y->c by hand to make a non-canonical value.
- item 2: the first version of the last block of set_rat_and_contains_rat_against_the_definition was
  nonsense (it compared a predicate with itself) and was replaced by the claim it should have made: for
  4/3 and m = 10 exactly one c in [0, 10) contains the rational, c = 8. Then the program hung: the loop
  variable c of the m = 1 block was overwritten by resid_pair, so the loop never ended. The loop
  variable is j now. The claim was not weakened.
- item 2: set_rat_statuses_and_shapes expected P(1, 0) after the DOMAIN calls of m = 4; the value there
  is P(4, 0), which is the point of the check. The expectation was corrected to m == 4.

