Note: the first run of forget_contains_every_rational_of_the_ball failed 234 checks. The test built
the ball with the raw triple (A, H, d) and then expected the modulus H and the condition gcd(d, H) = 1;
the function is documented on the canonical triple, and adf_fball_set_fmpz3 divides A, H, d by
gcd(A, H, d), so the test now reads the canonical triple with adf_fball_get_fmpz3 and makes its claims
about that. The second failure was a wrong membership formula of the test for 21/5: q is in
(a + H Zhat)/d exactly when (q d - a)/H is an integer, and the test had multiplied by the denominator
of q first. The claim (21/5 is in P(6, 3) and not in 3 + 6 Z) stands.

