Faults in the tests of item 4, found by the first green run and repaired in the test (no claim weakened):
- the first run failed 50012 checks. Two causes, both in the expected values of the test: (a) the
  round of a point was recovered with y = (sigma R d - n |T|)/m, which drops the sign; Proposition 1.5
  (2) gives y = (R d - sigma n |T|)/m; (b) the test compared against every solution of the enumeration,
  while the search visits the rounds x = 1, ..., min(X, ell) only, so it finds the solutions with
  x <= ell, which for a small limit is none. The test now sorts the list by (x, y) and cuts it at
  x > ell. The library was right in every one of the 50012 cases.
- the status counter of the test counted only the codes <= ADF_NOT_DETERMINED and so reported no
  NO_SOLUTION; the three counters are now by name.
- the vectors test did not know the status name DOMAIN at first; status_of now maps it.

