Faults in the tests of item 5, found by the first green run and repaired in the test:
- the first run reported 69022 accepted claims that the test called false. The test decided the truth
  of a claim as "the status of Algorithm R for this limit is that status", which is not what P1.11
  certifies: a claim of NOT_UNIQUE is true when the set has at least two elements and a claim of
  NO_SOLUTION is true when it is empty, whatever the limit says (P1.11 (1) and (2), and recon_truth of
  the reference, line 476). The test now decides the truth that way: OK needs q to be the only element,
  NO_SOLUTION needs the set empty, NOT_UNIQUE needs two elements, NOT_DETERMINED needs the four
  conditions of 1.7 (3). The library was right in every one of the 69022 cases.
- the vector test compared the status of the file (the status of recon_first) with the status of
  adf_resid_reconstruct; recon_first reports OK with a count, so the mapping count 2 -> NOT_UNIQUE and
  count 0 -> NOT_DETERMINED was missing.
- one comment of the test was left unterminated after that repair (a compile error, fixed).
